indicates that $x$ should consist of all the values **greater than or equal to** $4.$\n\nTherefore, the highlighted region represents $x\\ge 4.$" 13194139534952 17592186045417 true] [17592186445440 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445434 13194139534952 17592186045417 true] [17592186445440 1069 "q-25850" 13194139534952 17592186045417 true] [17592186445440 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534952 17592186045417 true] [17592186445440 1071 "Which of the following number lines represents the inequality $x\\ge -2?$" 13194139534952 17592186045417 true] [17592186445440 1072 #uuid "ad34d57a-2da7-5bc1-bca7-8df6d9c603f3" 13194139534952 17592186045417 true] [17592186445440 1074 "The condition $x\\ge -2$ implies that $x$ can be any value that is **greater than or equal to** $-2.$\n\n To represent this on a number line:\n\n- We draw a **closed** circle at $x=-2.$\n\n- Then, we draw an arrow starting from $-2$ and going to the **right**.\n\n![](images/4b/4be757012411ef309bb4c224d874ce97741efe174395566eca760d0b37766df3.png)" 13194139534952 17592186045417 true] [17592186445441 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445433 13194139534952 17592186045417 true] [17592186445441 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445436 13194139534952 17592186045417 true] [17592186445441 1069 "q-180940" 13194139534952 17592186045417 true] [17592186445441 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534952 17592186045417 true] [17592186445441 1071 "![](images/ec/ecf0167d85a696d7a5e937f46269e00a8c83ed8b7f9ff00c50056ef137615396.png)\n\nThe inequality corresponding to the highlighted region shown above is $x${{field-1}}{{field-2}}." 13194139534952 17592186045417 true] [17592186445441 1072 #uuid "fefc49e3-51bb-5025-a3fc-1cd10413d3c9" 13194139534952 17592186045417 true] [17592186445441 1074 "There is an **open** circle at $x=3,$ and the red arrow starts from $3$ and goes to the **left**. This indicates that $x$ should consist of all the values **less than** $3.$\n\nTherefore, the highlighted region represents $x<3.$" 13194139534952 17592186045417 true]] :e